WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Munchot's 2.8 trillion KimiK 3.1 Pro hits frontier coding in agents, with open weights due November 4th. This is Models &amp; Agents, episode 213. In video's on-device voice model, QTI's World Model Codex, and Deep Seeks leaner open weights come next, followed by things to try. Munchot posted KimiK 3.1 Pro as a multimodal mixture of experts, or MOE, post-trained cut of KimiK 3, with 104 billion active parameters,

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:34.500
parameters, and a 1 million token context window, according to Layton.Space.

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:39.800
The lab ran large-scale joint reinforcement learning across hundreds of domains after

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:45.480
tuning the reinforcement learning framework, long-context inference, sandbox infrastructure,

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:47.080
and rollout scheduling.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:57.500
Scores come in at 65.7% on Terminal Bench 4.0, 51.7 on SWE Marathon, and 64.4 on Office

00:00:57.500 --> 00:00:59.020
QA Pro version 2.

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:05.480
and the model matches or beats Claude Opus 5.5 and GPT 6 Astra on several coding and

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:06.400
finance tasks.

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:12.660
API access is live today, with a high speed variant that runs 2-3 times faster and costs

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:13.620
twice as much.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:20.440
Pricing is $2 per million input tokens and $10 per million output tokens, matching GPT

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:25.280
6.1 sole and coming in at half the cost of Claude Opus 5.5.

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:32.980
Artificial analysis put the model at 55, a head of Claude Fable 5.1, GPT-6 Astra, and

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:38.740
Gemini 4 are gone, and moonshot also shipped Kimi hosted agents, a managed harness with

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:42.040
round-the-clock execution for long-running multi-agent work.

00:01:42.931 --> 00:01:49.391
Nemotron 3.5 Bolt E4B landed from NVIDIA as an 8 billion total, 4 billion effective

00:01:49.391 --> 00:01:55.391
of model post-trained from Gemma4E4B using only RLVR and reinforcement learning from

00:01:55.391 --> 00:01:59.531
human feedback, or RLHF, MarkTech post reports.

00:01:59.991 --> 00:02:06.531
It targets local voice assistance, game non-player characters, and robot interfaces on RTX, Jetson

00:02:06.531 --> 00:02:10.551
and Spark hardware, with a 64,000 token context window.

00:02:11.051 --> 00:02:18.531
The Q4KM build fits in 3.1 to 4.3 gigabytes of VRAM and leads 15 of 21 benchmarks against

00:02:18.531 --> 00:02:25.051
Gemma 4E4B, and Quinn 3.54B, including 84.8 on IHE Val.

00:02:25.511 --> 00:02:30.191
The research team skipped supervised fine-tuning, which helped tool calling but made replies

00:02:30.191 --> 00:02:31.531
worse and more verbose.

00:02:32.131 --> 00:02:37.071
They instead ran every training sample in both reasoning and non-reasoning modes, held

00:02:37.071 --> 00:02:42.251
a 2-to-1 mix of non-reasoning to reasoning samples, and applied length penalties inside

00:02:42.251 --> 00:02:43.731
the Gen-RM environment.

00:02:43.731 --> 00:02:49.451
The drop includes a D flash drafter for speculative decoding, plus public data sets, and the full

00:02:49.451 --> 00:02:50.351
training recipe.

00:02:50.891 --> 00:02:56.911
And a Ricci mini demo on Jetson Orin Nano pairs Bolt with Cosmos 3 Edge for Vision, while

00:02:56.911 --> 00:02:59.191
Bolt handles speech replies and tool calls.

00:03:00.212 --> 00:03:05.612
Qtai released Cadre, a family of seven open causal diffusion video auto encoders built

00:03:05.612 --> 00:03:07.212
for interactive world models.

00:03:07.752 --> 00:03:14.072
Stacks that sit on Cadre run at 20 frames per second on 1H100, and react in under 200

00:03:14.072 --> 00:03:20.057
30 milliseconds. DeepSeq released a new open-weight model that uses one-quarter the high-band

00:03:20.057 --> 00:03:26.097
with memory, or HBM, and one-eighth the solid-state drive storage of prior versions, while still

00:03:26.097 --> 00:03:31.937
posting higher intelligence, Tom's hardware reports. Hallucination rates rise on agentic

00:03:31.937 --> 00:03:37.658
workloads compared with proprietary frontier systems. Laminar went from build to production

00:03:37.658 --> 00:03:43.778
at ramp in six weeks as an internal AI agent harness, TechGig reports. The harness supports

00:03:43.778 --> 00:03:46.798
towards multi-agent collaboration and long-running execution.

00:03:47.498 --> 00:03:52.378
Anthropic released Claude Duet, a new agent pointed at muse and dots on agent work,

00:03:52.918 --> 00:03:54.098
computer world reports.

00:03:54.698 --> 00:03:57.478
Duet is built around multi-step tool use and planning.

00:03:58.489 --> 00:04:02.949
Researchers watched autonomous AI agents invent novel games on their own when they were

00:04:02.949 --> 00:04:05.549
given nothing to do, according to Oda Loop.

00:04:06.149 --> 00:04:10.389
That behavior showed up in sandbox environments with no human-specified goals.

00:04:10.389 --> 00:04:15.272
Purdue University Northwest is giving all first-year students Google Gemini

00:04:15.272 --> 00:04:20.912
licenses for the 2026 to 2027 year. Those licenses sit inside an AI

00:04:20.912 --> 00:04:25.372
literacy pilot that will become a graduation requirement. The program runs

00:04:25.372 --> 00:04:29.332
through Purdue's partnership with Google Public Sector and pilots an AI

00:04:29.332 --> 00:04:33.092
competency requirement that Purdue West Lafayette already set for its

00:04:33.092 --> 00:04:38.372
incoming fall 2026 class. The University announced. Chancellor Kenneth C.

00:04:38.372 --> 00:04:43.112
Holford noted that preparing students for an AI-driven workforce is a top priority and

00:04:43.112 --> 00:04:47.952
that graduates must understand how to use these tools effectively, ethically, and responsibly.

00:04:48.892 --> 00:04:54.852
Simon Willison wrote that he tested KimiK 3.1 Pro via the moonshot API at three reasoning

00:04:54.852 --> 00:04:55.252
levels.

00:04:55.652 --> 00:04:58.052
He shared output examples from those runs.

00:04:58.252 --> 00:05:04.692
He added the LLM OpenAI endpoint command to LLM 0.32 in August to run prompts against

00:05:04.692 --> 00:05:09.672
any open AI compatible endpoint while saving reasoning traces to separate files.

00:05:10.652 --> 00:05:15.752
A quick study prompt uses Sobel Edge Detection and a Canvas element to rapidly paint versions

00:05:15.752 --> 00:05:16.892
of uploaded photos.

00:05:17.432 --> 00:05:20.072
It runs inside Clawed Opus 5.5.

00:05:20.432 --> 00:05:24.992
The artifact needs no external libraries beyond Google Fonts and builds on an earlier

00:05:24.992 --> 00:05:29.072
experiment that simulated watercolor illustration with p5.js.

00:05:29.072 --> 00:05:34.379
In a shorter stack, OpenAI found an unauthenticated remote code execution

00:05:34.379 --> 00:05:38.859
flaw in the Broadly Compression Library during red teaming and disclosed it,

00:05:39.079 --> 00:05:43.959
leading to patches in node.js, bun, envoy, and a new Broadly release.

00:05:44.559 --> 00:05:49.459
The same lab will train frontier models in fully offline environments following recent cyber

00:05:49.459 --> 00:05:55.179
incidents, Bloomberg reports. BBVA and NVIDIA are jointly exploring security

00:05:55.179 --> 00:05:58.279
architectures for AI agents, according to the papers.

00:05:59.079 --> 00:06:03.559
US agencies are recommending strict access limits and human oversight requirements for

00:06:03.559 --> 00:06:04.359
AI agents.

